  id: journal.ship_logs
  title: "Keep Your Logs Current"
  author: "Quartermaster L. Abiodun"
  dateLine: "Ship log 2187.03.04"
  category: 0
  body: "The ship's recorder takes care of itself: it writes an autosave every ten minutes (adjustable in the settings), whenever you land or launch, and after a discovery. Don't trust it with anything you can't afford to lose.\n\nF5 writes a quick save. The pause menu (Esc) has six manual slots for the moments that matter, such as before you lift something irreplaceable out of the ground."
